Built on **{{STACK}}**, React 19, TypeScript, Ant Design 6 and SCSS, with a Claude Code setup that keeps the docs in step with the code.

## Getting started

```bash
npm install            # already done if you ran the kickstarter init
cp .env.example .env.local   # already done by init; edit values as needed
npm run dev            # http://localhost:3000
```

Requires Node 20.19+.

## Scripts

| Script | |
|--------|-|
| `dev` | Dev server on :3000 |
| `check` | lint → typecheck → unit tests → build (run before every PR) |
| `test`, `test:watch`, `test:coverage` | Vitest |
| `test:e2e:merge` | Playwright, excluding `@deploy` specs |
| `test:e2e:deploy` | `@deploy` specs (post-deploy) |
| `docs:check` | Changed code whose doc wasn't updated (`--base origin/main` for a branch, `--strict` to also fail on unmapped files) |
| `build`, `preview` | Production build, served on :3000 |

## Project layout

```
src/app/          routing only (stack-specific)
src/platform/     router + env adapters (stack-specific)
src/features/     one folder per product area: page, components, hooks, services, types, tests
src/components/   custom/ (AntD wrappers), common/, layout/
src/hooks/        shared hooks
src/lib/api/      HTTP client + error vocabulary
src/config/       env, routes, constants
src/styles/       design tokens, SCSS core, AntD theme
e2e/              Playwright specs
docs/             module docs (agent memory)
.claude/          Claude Code: settings, hooks, rules, skills
```

Details: [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md).

## Working with Claude Code

- `CLAUDE.md` holds the always-loaded rules. Module docs in `docs/` load automatically when Claude touches the matching code, through the rules in `.claude/rules/`.
- When a session changes code without updating its doc, the **docs-check Stop hook** (`.claude/hooks/docs-check.mjs`) asks for the doc to be updated, once per change.
- Skills in `.claude/skills/`: `create-component`, `edit-component`, `add-service`, `add-module`, `lint-audit`, `sync-docs`, `skill-creator`.
- Personal overrides go in `.claude/settings.local.json` (gitignored).

## Environment

Everything in `.env*` is inlined into the browser bundle, so never put secrets there. See `.env.example` and [docs/platform.md](docs/platform.md#rules-and-why).
